an arts district staple is closing its  doors for reasons you may not think  martin's mart thrift shop on main street  near charleston has actually been a part  of that las vegas community since the  80s but madison kimbrough explains why  volunteers are now heartbroken over the  fact that they aren't going to be able  to stay open much longer madison  i've covered several stories in this  area many of which have to deal with the  expansion of the arts district but here  at martin's mart thrift shop as you can  see they are having to close their doors  due to high rent prices and lack of  support  it just like breaks my heart to see  something that's a legend that's been in  the same area  for 53 years and having to shut doors  for good martin's mart will be closing  its doors in november the volunteered  base thrift store is struggling to pay  rent originally paying just under a  thousand dollars it's now increased to  almost two thousand volunteer judy shock  says recently adding paid parking has  deterred shoppers and finding staff to  operate it is tough too we would like to  keep open  but i think the biggest thing that we  have no control over  and that is volunteers  you can't make someone volunteer many  former volunteers who grew up going to  the shop now have had to take a step  back after the pandemic having to  provide a steady income for themselves  and not being able to volunteer their  time like miles hoffman at 15 years old  i would ride my bike around the area and  i came up here i want to do whatever i  can to help save it move it what have  you whatever we can do you know it's a  vital resource i feel and in recent  months the city of las vegas announced  plans on expanding the arts district  area which for many store owners and  locals fear will mean higher rent and  the closure of more stores i'm afraid  that if it continues this isn't going to  be the the arts district that was built  on i think it's like trying to push out  the  little guys like this that kind of give  the neighborhood character  a gofundme has been created to help  martin's mart with rent fees in hopes  that they won't have to close down as of  now they are open three days a week and  we'll have a link to that gofundme page  up on our website at 8newsnow.com  reporting live in the arts district  madison kimbrough 8 news now
 

